#: {{synonyms|en|[[low#Adjective|low]] [[back pain]]|LBP|q2=abbreviation}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Francis Beeding [pseudonym; [[w:John Palmer (author)|John Palmer]]]|chapter=VII|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=C_CpBAAAQBAJ&pg=PT107|title=The Norwich Victims|location=London|publisher=Arcturus Publishing|year=1935|year_published=2013|section=section 2|isbn=978-1-78428-011-6|ol=245514W|passage=Sir Oswald Feiling winced as he turned to go home. He had felt a warning twinge of '''lumbago'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Gilbert Ryle|authorlink=Gilbert Ryle|chapter=Dilemma VII: Perception|title=Dilemmas: The {{w|Tarner Lectures}}, 1953|location=Cambridge, Cambridgeshire; New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|Cambridge University Press}}|year=1953|year_published=1954 (1987 printing)|page=105|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ka7oLeEgJ8kC&pg=PA105|isbn=978-0-521-06177-3|passage=We may imagine an athletics coach with a scientific training researching into the physiology and the psychology of runners. [...] He finds out the effects of fatigue, of alcohol, of tobacco, of '''lumbago''' and of depression upon their performances.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[episode]] of such backache.

